<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47791" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tentātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id.. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An attack</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">valetudinem tuam jam confirmatam esse et a
					vetere morbo et a novis tentationibus, gaudeo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 10, 17, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A trial</i>, <i>proof</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perseverantiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					4, 42, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">41, 23,
			14</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>Temptation</i> (eccl. Lat.), <i><span class="en">Vulg. Matt.
				6, 13</span></i> et saep. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
